1
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:05,178
Hi. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

2
00:00:05,178 --> 00:00:05,956
John Marchetta.

3
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:08,934
Sit down, sit down.

4
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:11,912
Susan has told me a great deal about you.

5
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,912
She says you're quite a man.

6
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:14,890
She says

7
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,868
a lot of wonderful things about you too, Mr. Stewart.

8
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:20,688
That's always nice to hear, Mr. Marchetta.

9
00:00:20,688 --> 00:00:21,513
Call me John.

10
00:00:21,513 --> 00:00:23,824
May I call you Malcolm?

11
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:25,624
Let's talk business.

12
00:00:25,624 --> 00:00:27,702
That's music to my ears.

13
00:00:27,702 --> 00:00:28,302
I understand

14
00:00:28,302 --> 00:00:33,716
you used to be in the construction business.

15
00:00:33,716 --> 00:00:34,978
Yup. Forty-three years.

16
00:00:34,978 --> 00:00:36,723
Here's a brief description

17
00:00:36,723 --> 00:00:42,549
of forty-three years of on-the-job training.

18
00:00:42,549 --> 00:00:44,669
That is some history!

19
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:47,647
You're a valuable asset, Malcolm.

20
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:48,647
Very valuable.

21
00:00:48,647 --> 00:00:50,625
Thank you.

22
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:53,978
Yup. Forty-three years.

23
00:00:53,978 --> 00:00:57,301
Half that time in my own construction company.

24
00:00:57,301 --> 00:01:01,039
Big jobs--factories, shopping malls.

25
00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:02,537
That kind of thing.

26
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:05,515
Then you retired.

27
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:06,115
Yes.

28
00:01:06,115 --> 00:01:08,493
After my wife died,

29
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:10,675
and I felt I should spend more time

30
00:01:10,675 --> 00:01:13,418
with my children and grandchildren.

31
00:01:13,418 --> 00:01:15,289
I lived in Florida,

32
00:01:15,289 --> 00:01:16,969
and they lived in New York.

33
00:01:16,969 --> 00:01:17,802
I understand.

34
00:01:17,802 --> 00:01:20,405
My dautghter Cami lives in New York.

35
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:23,383
I like being near her.

36
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:24,383
When I came here,

37
00:01:24,383 --> 00:01:26,361
I planned to take a few months off.

38
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:31,339
Relax with the family and then look for some work.

39
00:01:31,339 --> 00:01:33,817
Put my experience on the line ...

40
00:01:33,817 --> 00:01:35,628
but, unfortunately,

41
00:01:35,628 --> 00:01:39,130
there isn't any work for a retired person my age.

42
00:01:39,130 --> 00:01:40,416
Sometimes there is,

43
00:01:40,416 --> 00:01:48,751
and sometimes there isn't.

44
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:48,951
Well, I'm involved with an organization,

45
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:48,951
and we're trying to resolve that problem.

46
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:48,951
What's that?

47
00:01:48,751 --> 00:01:50,185
TOPS.

48
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:56,140
T-O-P-S--means Talented Older People's Society.

49
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:59,118
I'd like to be a member.

50
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:00,562
How much are the dues?

51
00:02:00,562 --> 00:02:02,096
There are no dues.

52
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:06,914
The organization serves major companies in this city.

53
00:02:06,914 --> 00:02:08,052
Why?

54
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:11,030
Because our members are men and women like you.

55
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:14,008
Experienced, talented, retired.

56
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:16,986
But our members want to go out there

57
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:18,306
and use their talents.

58
00:02:18,306 --> 00:02:19,964
They want to work.

59
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:22,942
That is fantastic, John!

60
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,920
I've got an idea for you, Malcolm.

61
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,527
Just fill out this form for me.

62
00:02:29,527 --> 00:02:29,727
It'll only take a few minutes.

63
00:02:29,527 --> 00:02:30,082
Sit right here,

64
00:02:30,082 --> 00:02:31,876
and do it while I talk to my secretary.

65
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:34,854
When I get back, we'll talk about my new factory.

66
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:38,261
My company is a member of TOPS.

67
00:02:38,261 --> 00:02:42,477
So I try hard to find opportunities for people like you.

68
00:02:42,477 --> 00:02:42,810
Malcolm.

69
00:02:42,810 --> 00:02:44,677
And when I see an opportunity,

70
00:02:44,677 --> 00:02:46,766
I can act on it.

71
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:52,722
Well, I can use your brainpower on the job right now.

72
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:53,991
Have you got time this morning

73
00:02:53,991 --> 00:02:56,300
to go over to the construction site with me?

74
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,678
I'd like to have you meet my foreman--

75
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:00,678
get some background on the job.

76
00:03:00,678 --> 00:03:01,656
I've got plenty of time.

77
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:04,634
I'll be right back.

78
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:46,992
We'll go over to the job site together.

79
00:03:46,992 --> 00:03:52,771
Malcolm, you worked on the Spaceport project?

80
00:03:52,771 --> 00:03:55,259
My company was the contractor.

81
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:56,739
I built the theater there

82
00:03:56,739 --> 00:03:58,607
with my own two hands, practically.

83
00:03:58,607 --> 00:03:59,347
I understand.

84
00:03:59,347 --> 00:03:59,717
Well,

85
00:03:59,717 --> 00:04:03,375
I'm glad to see you two guys getting along so well

86
00:04:03,375 --> 00:04:03,935
because, Danny,

87
00:04:03,935 --> 00:04:05,316
Malcolm is on the TOPS team.

88
00:04:05,316 --> 00:04:08,171
He's going to be working with you for a while.

89
00:04:08,171 --> 00:04:13,647
His experience will be valuable to both of us.

90
00:04:13,647 --> 00:04:14,427
Welcome aboard, Malcolm!

91
00:04:14,427 --> 00:04:15,787
I'm going back to my office.

92
00:04:15,787 --> 00:04:17,138
Give me a call later, Malcolm.

93
00:04:17,138 --> 00:04:20,012
I'll tell you the time and date of the next TOPS meeting.

94
00:04:20,012 --> 00:04:22,060
I'd like you to meet the group.

95
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:24,180
I will, John.

96
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,371
And again--thanks.

97
00:04:26,371 --> 00:04:29,296
No ... thank you.

98
00:04:29,296 --> 00:04:31,394
And thank Susan.

99
00:04:31,394 --> 00:04:33,972
He's quite a man.

100
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:35,452
A real inspiration for me.

101
00:04:35,452 --> 00:04:36,950
[04:07.02]OK, Danny.

102
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:41,378
I know you didn't expect to have me around,

103
00:04:41,378 --> 00:04:42,428
but I think I can be of some help to you.

104
00:04:42,428 --> 00:04:43,841
Let me tell you something, Malcolm.

105
00:04:43,841 --> 00:04:45,011
With your background and experience,

106
00:04:45,011 --> 00:04:45,884
I can learn something

107
00:04:45,884 --> 00:04:51,840
... and I do need some advice on a difficult problem.

108
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:53,507
Let me show you this.

109
00:04:53,507 --> 00:04:57,185
I don't want to give you a final opinion

110
00:04:57,185 --> 00:05:01,514
without studying these building plans more carefully.

111
00:05:01,514 --> 00:05:03,752
But a simple solution might be

112
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:05,480
to move the air-conditioning units

113
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,730
instead of redesigning the entire system.

114
00:05:07,730 --> 00:05:11,208
It might be simpler and less expensive .

115
00:05:11,208 --> 00:05:14,686
You just earned your weight in gold, Malcolm.

116
00:05:14,686 --> 00:05:18,642
Welcome aboard!

117
00:05:18,642 --> 00:05:21,620
It all happened so quickly!

118
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:23,620
I can't believe it!

119
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:26,278
I'm glad Mr. Marchetta was so helpful.

120
00:05:26,278 --> 00:05:27,576
He was more than helpful.

121
00:05:27,576 --> 00:05:30,554
He actually took me to meet his foreman.

122
00:05:30,554 --> 00:05:33,532
I'm thrilled for you, Grandpa.

123
00:05:33,532 --> 00:05:36,509
I don't know how to thank you, Susan.

124
00:05:36,509 --> 00:05:38,509
You're a wonderful granddaughter.

125
00:05:38,509 --> 00:05:40,487
It's good to see you so happy.

126
00:05:40,487 --> 00:05:42,842
I'll be at the construction site tomorrow.

127
00:05:42,842 --> 00:05:45,265
What are you doing tomorrow night?

128
00:05:45,265 --> 00:05:46,943
I'm not doing anything.

129
00:05:46,943 --> 00:05:47,443
Why?

130
00:05:47,443 --> 00:05:49,107
How about a date with your grandfather?

131
00:05:49,107 --> 00:05:52,134
I owe you a good steak dinner.

132
00:05:52,134 --> 00:05:54,377
I'll accept.

133
00:05:54,377 --> 00:05:55,257
Tomorrow night.

134
00:05:55,257 --> 00:05:57,017
You and me. Dinner.

135
00:05:57,017 --> 00:05:57,355
What time?

136
00:05:57,355 --> 00:06:00,333
I'll pick you up here at seven .

137
00:06:00,333 --> 00:06:01,333
Is that OK?

138
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:03,093
I can't wait!

139
00:06:03,093 --> 00:06:03,811
And you can tell me

140
00:06:03,811 --> 00:06:06,289
all about your first full day back on the job.

141
00:06:06,289 --> 00:06:09,289
It's a deal!
